# Saajha Nirman — Premium Silver & Emerald Green Frontend

## 1. Project Overview

Build a polished, responsive, production-quality frontend for **Saajha Nirman**, a sustainable construction-material recovery and exchange platform.

**Tagline:** “Waste Less. Build More. Together.”

**Problem statement:** Small construction projects often leave usable construction materials such as bricks, tiles, pipes, timber, cement boards, doors, fittings, and other supplies unused. At the same time, nearby projects purchase the same materials, creating unnecessary expenses and construction waste.

**Solution:** Saajha Nirman connects construction sites with surplus materials to nearby sites requesting those materials. It recommends feasible transfers based on material type, quantity, condition, geographic distance, and pickup deadline.

**Core differentiator:** This is a material recovery and waste-diversion workflow, not a generic buy-and-sell marketplace. The platform should show how much material was reused, how much surplus remains, how many transfers were completed, and how much waste was potentially diverted.

The provided reference image is the layout inspiration. Recreate its overall information architecture—sidebar navigation, dashboard cards, material listings, listing creation forms, material detail pages, requests, matching recommendations, transfers, and analytics—but redesign the visual language to feel premium, modern, minimal, and distinctive.

